WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
Millions were reportedly stolen from polymarket users, forcing a trading halt. This is prediction

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:10.680
market's daily episode 38. Journalism and education never a bet. After that, a warning

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:15.460
out of Australia, pressure from two senators and a look at collateral that cannot move until

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:20.440
a market pays. Bloomberg reported the halt after customers were said to have lost money.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:25.780
Gizmodo reported a temporary freeze, with the theft running through a third-party service.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:31.200
The Defiant reported that Polymarket also paused its re-layer while the incident was open.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.140
The Wall Street Journal reported that some users said funds were drained.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:39.580
Business Insider reported that Polymarket is investigating a potential hack.

00:00:40.933 --> 00:00:45.213
Australia's securities regulator is the next actor, and the date is October 30.

00:00:45.733 --> 00:00:50.793
Law 360 reported that the Australian Securities and Investments Commission warned these markets

00:00:50.793 --> 00:00:53.193
mirror binary options the country has banned.

00:00:53.193 --> 00:00:58.853
Finance Magnates reported that the commission is not backing prediction markets for retail clients.

00:00:59.413 --> 00:01:02.393
FX News Group reported that the commission put out a statement.

00:01:02.913 --> 00:01:08.130
The jurisdiction is Australia. David Woodcock, the SEC's enforcement director,

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:11.130
told Bloomberg the agency is watching these markets.

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:17.290
crypto.news reported on October 29th. He said the commission has to be ready when people commit fraud

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:23.290
or other securities violations. He put enforcement in the future for sure, and he named no company

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:24.810
and announced no new charges.

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:29.530
The comments centered on contracts tied to company earnings and other performance figures.

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:35.050
The SEC has approved a SIBO proposal for binary options on measures such as earnings

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:39.330
and sales, and that order did not make every performance contract a security.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:46.050
In June, the SEC and the CFTC asked the public how to classify swaps, security-based swaps

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:47.470
and products that mixed the two.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:53.090
A CFTC interim rule that keeps casino-style gambling products out of the swap definition

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.610
took effect on October 19th.

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:59.570
Comments on a separate proposal to pull certain event contracts into that definition

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:01.924
are due November 18th.

00:02:01.924 --> 00:02:06.784
Senators Warren and Curtis are pressing Kalshi and Polly Market on election market safeguards.

00:02:07.224 --> 00:02:09.164
The Hill described the pair as bipartisan.

00:02:09.904 --> 00:02:15.004
The Defiant reported a November 3 deadline for answers, including how many suspected election

00:02:15.004 --> 00:02:17.764
trading violations were stopped before a trade went through.

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:22.211
Kalshi raised $1 billion at a $40 billion valuation.

00:02:22.891 --> 00:02:26.251
CityBiz framed that round as coming ahead of a likely IPO.

00:02:26.911 --> 00:02:29.411
That is a characterization of the raise, not a filing.

00:02:30.031 --> 00:02:33.831
Markets Media reported the same billion dollar raise and the same valuation.

00:02:34.531 --> 00:02:37.271
Shattered.io described the round as a series G.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:41.600
Coinbase's third quarter net income jumped 66%.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:42.900
The block reported.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:47.580
Bernstein analysts told the block that growing prediction markets and derivatives helped

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.200
offset weaker spot trading.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:54.720
Biggo Finance reported that, on the earnings call, prediction markets hit a $200 million

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:55.600
run rate.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:03:01.320
That same account said the business offset a 10% drop in spot volume, with revenue flat

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:02.420
from the prior quarter.

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:07.863
In short, the Indian Gaming Association raised prediction market concerns at the USET

00:03:07.863 --> 00:03:08.583
annual meeting.

00:03:09.143 --> 00:03:14.783
The CFTC set on October 29th that it had held its first frontier forum on superintelligence

00:03:14.783 --> 00:03:19.343
the day before, covering that technology in derivatives markets and agentic trading.

00:03:19.343 --> 00:03:24.463
trading. Trading View reported that Robin Hood's crypto revenue fell 55% while prediction

00:03:24.463 --> 00:03:29.643
markets supported growth. CalShi has sued Missouri as well as Louisiana over sports

00:03:29.643 --> 00:03:34.903
wagering laws. Vital law reported in the Eastern District of Missouri and the Western District

00:03:34.903 --> 00:03:41.459
of Louisiana. Those are filings, not rulings. Which party wins the House in 2026 is on the

00:03:41.459 --> 00:03:48.159
board today, with the Democratic Party at 93.5% on Polly Market. On CalShi, a Democratic

00:03:48.159 --> 00:03:53.439
sweep of Congress is priced at 68 percent, up three points from the previous day's price.

00:03:54.039 --> 00:03:59.859
A contract that the U.S. Iran ceasefire continues through October 31st is at 91 percent on

00:03:59.859 --> 00:04:07.159
polymarket, down 5.8 points in a day. On Calche, Democratic control of the Senate is at 68 percent.

00:04:07.799 --> 00:04:13.559
Benjamin Netanyahu leads the polymarket question on Israel's next prime minister at 40.5 percent,

00:04:13.559 --> 00:04:19.619
down 5 points in a day. Say implied probability once and leave it there. Each of those figures

00:04:19.619 --> 00:04:24.659
is a price, not a forecast from this show. Whether these venues are available and for which

00:04:24.659 --> 00:04:29.519
contracts depends on where you live. The rules differ by country, province and state

00:04:29.519 --> 00:04:34.827
and they are changing. On the week's board, Polly Markets Democrats sweep contract in

00:04:34.827 --> 00:04:42.087
the midterm balance of power market sat at 66.5% on Sunday and the same 66.5% on Thursday,

00:04:42.087 --> 00:04:48.667
a move of zero points. The contract that the U.S. Iran ceasefire last through October 31st moved

00:04:48.667 --> 00:04:57.227
from 82.5% on Sunday to 85.5% on Monday, up three points on Polly Market. The Democratic Party in

00:04:57.227 --> 00:05:05.147
the House Market moved from 91.5% on Monday to 92.5% on Thursday, up one point on Polly Market.

00:05:05.147 --> 00:05:13.607
Gaddi Eisenkot in the Israeli Prime Minister market moved from 56.6% on Monday to 59.5% on Tuesday,

00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:21.486
up 2.9 points on Polly Market. 14 other questions were read once this week. Polly Market has listed a

00:05:21.486 --> 00:05:26.746
market on which coalition forms the next Israeli government. That asks about the governing block,

00:05:27.006 --> 00:05:32.046
not only who holds the Prime Minister's office. Today's readings do not carry a price for that

00:05:32.046 --> 00:05:37.966
contract. Locked collateral is how it works between a trade and a payout. The dollar cannot

00:05:37.966 --> 00:05:43.366
leave until an oracle settles the claim. A paper on settlement discounting says a near-certain

00:05:43.366 --> 00:05:48.726
dollar in that setup is a delayed dollar. The price then holds a belief about the outcome

00:05:48.726 --> 00:05:54.146
and a separate discount for the wait until cash. The authors pull that second piece from contracts

00:05:54.146 --> 00:05:58.866
that stay near-certain, using the settlement times those contracts actually realized.

00:05:58.866 --> 00:06:02.426
They summarize the curve as an annualized settlement wedge.

00:06:02.966 --> 00:06:04.986
The wedges they recover are positive.

00:06:05.486 --> 00:06:08.086
They change with maturity and they change over time.

00:06:08.746 --> 00:06:12.126
Take the raw prices of those near certain claims across horizons.

00:06:12.646 --> 00:06:17.426
The horizon gradient is how far those prices drift as the weight until settlement gets longer.

00:06:18.066 --> 00:06:20.126
Adjust the prices by the recovered curves.

00:06:20.606 --> 00:06:26.226
The paper finds that step cuts the near certainty horizon gradient by roughly 48-88%.

00:06:26.226 --> 00:06:31.826
On that measure, most of the raw pattern across maturities is a priced weight, not forecast

00:06:31.826 --> 00:06:32.686
error alone.

00:06:33.206 --> 00:06:35.846
What is left is the slice the wedge does not explain.

00:06:36.606 --> 00:06:41.326
Neg-risk conversion compresses the discounts by recycling part of the position into synthetic

00:06:41.326 --> 00:06:44.666
collateral, so less capital sits idle for the whole weight.

00:06:45.346 --> 00:06:50.046
Yield-bearing collateral flattens the term structure by cutting the opportunity cost of the lockup.

00:06:50.586 --> 00:06:54.226
The dollar that cannot be withdrawn can still earn something while it waits.

00:06:54.226 --> 00:06:59.526
In both designs, the price moves because the funding terms moved, not because the event

00:06:59.526 --> 00:07:01.046
became more or less likely.

00:07:01.666 --> 00:07:04.286
The paper does not say the wedge erases the gradient.

00:07:04.766 --> 00:07:07.666
A cut of 48% to 88% leaves a remainder.

00:07:08.306 --> 00:07:12.286
The measurement is also tied to collateral locked until an oracle redeems the claim.

00:07:12.966 --> 00:07:18.166
A venue that pays from a different custody setup, or that turns capital over sooner, sits

00:07:18.166 --> 00:07:19.246
outside these curves.

00:07:19.866 --> 00:07:21.806
The limit is the one the measurement states.

00:07:21.806 --> 00:07:26.746
A price near certainty means something different once you know when the dollar can actually leave.

00:07:27.186 --> 00:07:32.006
A contract that is already sure, but whose collateral cannot move until a later oracle date,

00:07:32.406 --> 00:07:35.566
is not the same object as a contract that settles at once.

00:07:36.046 --> 00:07:41.326
Part of the gap can be the weight, what the collateral earns, and whether the market recycles capital,

00:07:41.866 --> 00:07:43.846
rather than a different belief about the event.

00:07:44.406 --> 00:07:49.966
The paper's closing claim is that these prices aggregate information through funding conditions that can be measured.

